{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.lemma_generator_choice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.lemma_generator_choice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.lemma_generator_choice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.lemma_generator_choice","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/lemma_generator_choice.lean#L48-L82","doc":"**Generator choice — multi-step division run.**\n\nFor any division run `f →* g` (`MultiStepReduction`): either no step\nwas taken (`f = g`), or there is an intermediate element `g'` with\n`f →* g'`, a final single step `g' → g`, and that step is realised by\na genuine basis generator `r ∈ sys.rules`. So every nontrivial run\nuses a member of `G` — the manuscript's \"we may take `hᵢ = g_{γᵢ}`\".\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete disjunction over the reduction\nrelation** (an equality on `AlgElement`, or an existential producing\n`r ∈ sys.rules` and the witnessing subword occurrence), not a bare\n`Prop`. Proved by `cases` on the reduction derivation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:ugb-generator-choice","label":"lem:ugb-generator-choice","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/lemma-generator-choice.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}